45. FILE ALLOCATION METHODS ⭐⭐⭐

Important methods:

1. Contiguous allocation

File blocks are stored together.

10 11 12 13 14

Advantages:

fast sequential access
fast direct access

Problem:

external fragmentation
difficult file growth
2. Linked allocation

Each block points to the next block.

10 → 25 → 7 → 18

Advantage:

no need for contiguous blocks

Disadvantage:

poor/random access
3. Indexed allocation

An index block stores pointers to file blocks.

Index Block
 ↓
10
25
7
18

Good for direct access.

